tests read the body of a HEAD response through `fastify.inject()`:\n\n- \"Should allow registering a constrained GET route after a constrained\nHEAD route\" (`test/constrained-routes.test.js`) checks `res.payload ===\n'custom HEAD response'`;\n- \"fastify.all should add all the methods to the same url\"\n(`test/internals/all.test.js`) parses the HEAD payload as JSON.\n\nA real server sends no body for HEAD, and fastify/light-my-request#408\nmakes `inject()` do the same. @gurgunday approved the behaviour there\nbut asked for fastify core to be updated before it ships, since these\ntwo tests would fail with it.\n\nThese tests now check the response headers instead of the body:\n\n- The constrained route test asserts the `content-type` set by the\ncustom HEAD handler (`text/plain`) and the `content-length` of `'custom\nHEAD response'`. That still shows the custom handler ran, not a HEAD\nroute derived from the GET one.\n- The `fastify.all` test asserts the HEAD response's `content-length`\nmatches `JSON.stringify({ method: 'HEAD' })` and parses the body only\nfor the other methods.\n\nBoth files pass with the current light-my-request release and with the\n#408 branch symlinked into `node_modules` (26 tests each time), so this\ncan land before or after it. ESLint is clean on both files.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 78d68b2225baa3b7e05ebb5522239f40a4bcf6e8)","timestamp":"2026-10-24T15:13:13Z","author":{"name":"Alperen","email":"manasalperen@gmail.com"},"committer":{"name":"Antonio Tripodi","email":"Tony133@users.noreply.github.com"}},"repository":{"id":69495170,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk2OTQ5NTE3MA==","name":"fastify","full_name":"fastify/fastify","private":false,"owner":{"login":"fastify","id":24939410,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjI0OTM5NDEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24939410?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fastify","html_url":"https://github.com/fastify","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fastif